  where: "The death cap comes from Europe. It has spread to North America, Australia, and other places, usually by hitching a ride on the roots of imported trees like oaks. It has a greenish-yellow cap, white gills, a ring on the stem, and a cup at the base. It can be mistaken for edible mushrooms, like the paddy straw mushrooms eaten in Asia.",
